[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### Step 4: For Each Valid Triplet, Count the Number of Assignments
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m We are to count the number of **assignments** of flavors to players, where:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - Each player gets one flavor (chocolate, vanilla, or strawberry)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - Each flavor is used at least once
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - The counts $ c, v, s $ match the triplet
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m This is a **multinomial coefficient**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m For a given triplet $ (c, v, s) $, the number of ways to assign flavors is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m \frac{9!}{c! \, v! \, s!}
