[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m > **Find the sum of all integer bases $ b > 9 $ for which $ 17_b $ is a divisor of $ 97_b $.**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the notation
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m In base $ b $, the number $ 17_b $ means:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 1 \cdot b + 7 = b + 7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m Similarly, the number $ 97_b $ means:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 9 \cdot b + 7 = 9b + 7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m So we are looking for **integer bases $ b > 9 $** such that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m b + 7 \text{ divides } 9b + 7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### Step 2: Set up the divisibility condition
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m We want:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m b + 7 \mid 9b + 7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m This means:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### Step 3: Use modular arithmetic
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m We can write:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 9b + 7 \equiv 0 \pmod{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m Divide $ 9b + 7 $ by $ b + 7 $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m \frac{9b + 7}{b + 7} = \frac{9(b + 7) - 63 + 7}{b + 7} = \frac{9(b + 7) - 56}{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m \frac{9b + 7}{b + 7} = 9 - \frac{56}{b + 7}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m For this to be an integer, $ \frac{56}{b + 7} $ must be an integer.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m b + 7 \mid 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### Step 4: Find all $ b > 9 $ such that $ b + 7 \mid 56 $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m We need to find all positive integers $ d $ such that:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m d \mid 56 \quad \text{and} \quad b = d - 7 > 9
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m d - 7 > 9 \Rightarrow d > 16
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m So we look for divisors of 56 that are **greater than 16**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### Step 5: List all divisors of 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m The divisors of 56 are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 1, 2, 4, 7, 8, 14, 28, 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m Now find which of these are **greater than 16**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 28, 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m So the valid values of $ d $ are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m d = 28, 56
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### Step 6: Find corresponding $ b $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m b = d - 7
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m For $ d = 28 $:
