[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### **Step 1: Understand the triangle areas**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m We are given that for each $ i = 2, 3, \ldots, 10 $, the area of $ \triangle A_i A_1 A_{i+1} $ is **1**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - $ \vec{A_1 A_2} = \vec{u} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - $ \vec{A_1 A_3} = \vec{v} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - $ \vec{A_1 A_4} = \vec{w} $
