[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 1. When she walks at speed $ s $, the total time (walk + coffee shop) is 240 minutes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 2. When she walks at speed $ s + 2 $, the total time (walk + coffee shop) is 144 minutes.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m Let’s write the equations.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### Step 2: Write the equations for the two scenarios
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m #### Case 1: Speed $ s $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - Distance = 9 km
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - Time = 240 minutes = 4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - So, the time she spends walking is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m   $$
