[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m [response] We are given the following information:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - Aya walks **9 kilometers** each morning.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - She walks at a **constant speed of $ s $ kilometers per hour**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - The **total time** for the walk (including the $ t $ minutes spent in the coffee shop) is **4 hours**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - When she walks at a speed of $ s + 2 $ kilometers per hour, the total time is **2 hours and 24 minutes**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - We are to find the **total time** for a walk at a speed of $ s + \frac{1}{2} $ kilometers per hour, **including the $ t $ minutes spent in the coffee shop**.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### Step 1: Convert all times to hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m We are given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - 4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - 2 hours and 24 minutes = $ 2 + \frac{24}{60} = 2 + 0.4 = 2.4 $ hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - Time at speed $ s $: 4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - Time at speed $ s + 2 $: 2.4 hours
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### Step 2: Write the distance formula
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m The distance is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m \text{Distance} = \text{Speed} \times \text{Time}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m We know the distance is 9 kilometers, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m #### At speed $ s $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 9 = s \times 4 \Rightarrow s = \frac{9}{4} = 2.25 \text{ km/h}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m #### At speed $ s + 2 $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 9 = (s + 2) \times 2.4
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m Substitute $ s = 2.25 $:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 9 = (2.25 + 2) \times 2.4 = 4.25 \times 2.4
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m Calculate:
