[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - Circumcenter $ O $ at the origin: $ O = (0, 0) $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - Incenter $ I $ at some point $ (x, y) $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - $ \overline{IA} \perp \overline{OI} $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m This gives us a geometric condition:  
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m \vec{IA} \cdot \vec{OI} = 0
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m Let’s denote:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - $ A = (x_A, y_A) $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - $ I = (x_I, y_I) $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - $ O = (0, 0) $
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m Then:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m - $ \vec{IA} = (x_A - x_I, y_A - y_I) $
