[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### Step 11: Use the formula for the area of the triangle
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m We have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m A = r \cdot s = 6s
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m Also, from the **law of sines**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m \frac{a}{\sin A} = 2R = 26 \Rightarrow a = 26 \sin A
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m a = 26 \sin A
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m We know:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m \cos A = \frac{13}{24} \Rightarrow \sin A = \sqrt{1 - \left( \frac{13}{24} \right)^2} = \sqrt{1 - \frac{169}{576}} = \sqrt{\frac{407}{576}} = \frac{\sqrt{407}}{24}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m So:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m a = 26 \cdot \frac{\sqrt{407}}{24} = \frac{26 \sqrt{407}}{24} = \frac{13 \sqrt{407}}{12}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ---
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m ### Step 12: Use the formula for the semi-perimeter
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m We also have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m $$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=14021)[0m A = 6s \Rightarrow s = \frac{A}{6}
